# Default-deny build context.
#
# Both Dockerfiles in this repository copy whole directories -- `COPY . .` in
# ./Dockerfile and `COPY . $SRC/ovumcy-sync-community` in
# .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile -- and `docker build` reads this file from the
# context root for every build that uses that root. Without it the context
# carries the entire working tree to the daemon: `.git` with full history,
# local agent worktrees under `.claude/`, the gitignored `data/` SQLite
# database, editor and tooling state. All of it lands in the build cache, and
# any of it can be baked into a layer by a wildcard COPY.
#
# So: deny everything, then re-include exactly what a build reads.
*

# Module graph. ./Dockerfile runs `COPY go.mod go.sum ./` before `go mod
# download` so dependency resolution caches independently of the sources.
!go.mod
!go.sum

# The Go trees `go build ./cmd/ovumcy-sync-community` compiles.
#
# `*_test.go` is included on purpose: .clusterfuzzlite/build.sh compiles the
# fuzz targets (FuzzNormalizeLogin, FuzzParseClientIP, ...) and every one of
# them lives in a _test.go file.
!cmd/**/*.go
!internal/**/*.go

# Schema migrations, embedded into the binary by internal/db (`//go:embed
# migrations/*.sql`) -- a missing .sql here is a build failure, not a runtime
# one.
!internal/db/migrations/*.sql

# .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile copies its own build script out of the context.
!.clusterfuzzlite/**
